<title>CANADA: Canada M1 money supply rises in August.</title>
<headline>Canada M1 money supply rises in August.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian M1 money supply rose by C$451 million to C$63.47 billion in August from C$63.02 billion in July and compared with C$57.73 billion in August 1995, the Bank of Canada said on Friday.</p>
<p>					   Aug 96    July 96     Aug 95</p>
<p>M1					 63.47	63.02	57.73</p>
<p>M2					389.10     389.79     380.70</p>
<p>M3					482.44     482.13     462.46</p>
<p>Note - Figures are unadjusted, in billions of dollars.  </p>
<p>Chartered bank assets			    Aug	  July</p>
<p>   Net foreign currency			-11.12	-12.63</p>
<p>   Canadian dollar			     640.31	639.55</p>
<p>   Total Canadian liquid assets	    102.94	107.83</p>
<p>				  Wk to Sept 18 Chg on wk    Chg on yr</p>
<p>Notes in circulation		 26.900  -0.340	+0.534</p>
<p>Government cash balances	    4.494  -3.080	-4.996</p>
<p>Govt securities outstanding     463.392  -2.759	+6.579</p>
<p>Treasury bills			151.600  -0.600     -16.000</p>
<p>Canada saving bonds		  30.020  -0.022	+0.634</p>
<p>    All figures in billions of dollars.</p>
</text>
